<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Bos taurus Gierer–Meinhardt wavelength at 3.137 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Bos taurus)",
        "Bos taurus Gierer–Meinhardt wavelength at 3.137 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Bos taurus morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Bos taurus specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Bos taurus" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a cryptographic nanopublication. No nanopub profile was present.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the Fleckvieh patches are the 3.137 µm mode. That animal is a second segmentation voucher only.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the sibling Holstein flank model.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pearson r = 0.99595, RMSE = 0.104 µm, KS = 0.414, two foreground fractions that are not equal to each other or to the simulated occupancy.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Same calibrated Gierer–Meinhardt integration as pass 1, plus the scale-neighbour annotation, a second segmented Bos taurus voucher, and activator-only growth frames.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) and Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) supply the dispersion relation and the activator–inhibitor kinetics.",
        "reported_in_source: Wasmeier et al. (2008) place melanosomes below 1 µm. Murray (1981) is the macroscopic coat claim this slot does not repeat.",
        "transfer_boundary: Neither photograph resolves 3.137 µm. The wavelength is the calibrated k_star, not a ruler on the image.",
        "transfer_boundary: No predecessor chronospecies is in the slot. The age offset along the series is zero." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/bos_taurus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Bos taurus; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) and Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) supply the dispersion relation and the activator–inhibitor kinetics. | Wasmeier et al. (2008) place melanosomes below 1 µm. Murray (1981) is the macroscopic coat claim this slot does not repeat.; reconstructed_in_script: Same calibrated Gierer–Meinhardt integration as pass 1, plus the scale-neighbour annotation, a second segmented Bos taurus voucher, and activator-only growth frames. | Pearson r = 0.99595, RMSE = 0.104 µm, KS = 0.414, two foreground fractions that are not equal to each other or to the simulated occupancy.; transfer_boundary: Neither photograph resolves 3.137 µm. The wavelength is the calibrated k_star, not a ruler on the image. | No predecessor chronospecies is in the slot. The age offset along the series is zero.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the Fleckvieh patches are the 3.137 µm mode. That animal is a second segmentation voucher only. | Does not claim a cryptographic nanopublication. No nanopub profile was present. | Does not claim the sibling Holstein flank model.]; phenomenon_size: 9.5 mm (0.00946 m, log10=-2.024 m, tier=6_organ_mm); species_scale_ladder (2 runs from 9.5 mm to 50 cm): 9.5 mm:airway-mucosal-creasing, 50 cm:bos-taurus-turing-wavelength" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/jcs.040667> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
